<h3 id="unisul">Unisul Virtual - Palhoça/SC <span>2005 — 2008</span></h3>

<h4>Administrative Assistant in Materials Logistics</h4>

<p>Working in the Materials Logistics department was a highly enriching experience, characterized by a unique and challenging dynamic. Some days were intensely busy, with a flood of requests, while others were much calmer. It was during these quieter periods that the idea arose to develop a Material Dispatch Control System to replace the inefficient Excel spreadsheets.</p>

<p>Later, I implemented an online protocol system that allowed the administrative office to request materials directly via the internet. Besides simplifying the process, this solution enabled real-time tracking of each request, eliminating email overload and speeding up the resolution of student issues.</p>

<p>I also created a new label model that made envelope customization easier. This model not only simplified material registration but also integrated the delivery tracking process, linking it with the Brazilian Postal Service (Correios) and Unisul’s internal system. Today, when users receive a package with a label containing both the delivery and return addresses, they are benefiting from this innovation that originated at UnisulVirtual.</p>

<p>I further developed an automated label generation system that classified students according to predefined criteria, as well as a solution to monitor material returns sent through the postal service. This system automated email notifications and return logging, preventing addressing errors and optimizing postal costs by avoiding the shipment of books to incorrect addresses.</p>

<p>These innovations were presented at the Distance Education Seminar on 10/29/2007 and can be viewed in the document <a href="https://eduardokraus.com/eduardo/arquivos/Artigo_Seminario_EAD.pdf" target="_blank">Artigo_Seminario_EAD.pdf</a>.</p>

<p>In addition, at the request of the Evaluation team, I developed specific modules within the internal system to enhance the department’s performance. We created a test control system that included automatic generation of meeting minutes, random question selection, test formatting, tracking management, reporting, and an intelligent label to facilitate the control and archiving of received tests.</p>

<p>These innovations not only simplified our daily tasks but also improved the overall quality of services provided, making the process more efficient and agile.</p>

